{"description": null, "did_you_know": null, "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "Artist's inscription, signature, and seal:

White clouds surround red trees; 
Mist has already returned to the valley.
Why not rest and let your mind be at peace with the world.
With solidarity ch'in [lute] sit in the river pavilion.
An old friend is expected but doesn't show up;
The day is cold, with maple leaves falling.

In the wu-shen year [1788], Erh-ch'iao shan-jen, Li Chien copies and inscribes. [seal] Li Chien Chih yin.  trans. HK/LYSL", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": null}], "citations": [], "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60472309"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1972.42-white-clouds-and-red"]}}
